    "result_text": "The full suite (BUILD SUCCESS, all tests passing) is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule: an owner's `membershipTier` becomes `GOLD` when their household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3 or more members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nFollowing the existing patterns for derived owner fields (`namesakeCount`, `bulkSignupWarning`), I put each piece of logic where it belongs:\n\n- **`MembershipTierFormatter`** (`util/`) \u2014 the single home for tier derivation. `format` now takes `householdSize` first and returns `GOLD` when it's \u2265 3 (constant `GOLD_HOUSEHOLD_SIZE`), otherwise falls through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n- **`Owner`** (`model/`) \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with getter/setter, alongside the existing snapshot fields.\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner`** \u2014 sets `householdSize = householdMembers.size() + 1` (existing household members plus the new owner) at create time, reusing the already-computed `findHouseholdMembers` result rather than re-querying.\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 updated the mapping expression to pass `owner.getHouseholdSize()` into the formatter.\n- **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `household_size INTEGER` column.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD tier.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` and the full suite pass (BUILD SUCCESS).",
